    "created_at": "2026-11-24T19:42:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T19:42:56Z",
    "body": "> For images that don't have a natural size, like dimensionless SVG images or an `<img>` with `content: linear-gradient(...)`, its unclear what to do here.\n> \n> For the most part, places where images need to be sized and displayed in some way like this should specify a [concrete object size resolution](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#concrete-size-resolution) algorithm to use.\n\nI think it makes sense to use a concrete layout sizing that is derived from layout in such cases.\n\nImplementation note: if an `Element` is passed to `setDragImage` that is not an `HTMLImageElement`, Chromium uses the bounds and contents of the containing stacking context of that element to size and raster the drag image.",
